# COALSHARD feasibility and stop report — 2026-09-10

## Outcome

Part 1 found that the stored physics contains the default evaluation and unilateral/single-user counterfactual evaluations, but no joint evaluation whose changed set has size two or greater. The declared target

`Psi_A = Delta F(A) - sum_{i in A} d_i`

therefore cannot be recovered from this physics layer. `Delta F(A)` must come from the real joint evaluation of the configuration changed on exactly `A`; it cannot be reconstructed from singleton outcomes. Part 2 was stopped as required. No coalition JSONL, sidecar, sealed physics file, source view, build state, or `EXACTGEN2`-owned path was created, changed, moved, or deleted.

This report is the only file emitted by COALSHARD.

## Verified by running code

### Physics inventory and stored quantities

The snapshot was read from `artifacts/v025-exact-source-20260910-BUILD_NOT_CLAIM/.staging-separated-v1`. SHA-256 sidecar verification passed for all 15 physics shards and all 15 existing view shards.

