The scorer passed, but my independent provenance cross-check caught one reuse defect: when a PANELCEIL reference had the same assignment as the base under a different configuration ID, the producer recomputed that base outcome instead of taking PANELCEIL’s stored endpoint. Eleven anchors matched exactly; one exposed the issue. I’m correcting the lookup to key by physical assignments and regenerating the affected bytes before treating the panel as final.
