+**Panel `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.json` contains 20 anchors, uses first improvement in ascending-user/declared-option order with ordered microbatches of 16, and the real scorer dry-run verdict is PASS (exit 0; synthetic fixture smoke only, not evidence).**
+
+# PANELBUILD — Stage-C scoring-panel producer and receipt
+
+## Outcome
+
+The producer is [`scripts/build_stagec_scoring_panel.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/scripts/build_stagec_scoring_panel.py). It emitted:
+
+- panel: [`artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.json`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.json), SHA-256 `071175d2198bd3a176e2615438be99febba22fee624d17c0bc0f98746dad1ccc`;
+- panel sidecar: [`artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.json.sha256`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.json.sha256);
+- construction receipt: [`artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.receipt.json`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/artifacts/stagec-scoring-panel-first20-v1.receipt.json), SHA-256 `f45242da2937a4518c2941d9d4a09f422d2dbb63ea7518f4026f1f1490ac498f`.
+
+The panel contains one common ordered catalogue per anchor. There is no arm-specific profile inventory: all five arms score the same `profiles` array, ordered with the base first and then by stable physical configuration ID before the IDs are SHA-256-shortened. Across the 20 anchors there are 19,780 profiles (963 minimum and 1,009 maximum per anchor), and no full-horizon profile was rejected as physically invalid.
+
+Every profile carries C1 selected/reference states, C2 selected/reference states, the C3 coalition state, and its declared full-buffer physical outcome. Outcomes use all 48 realised boundaries and contain decoded bits, partial-payload DC joules, rate-target attainment/opportunities, service availability/opportunities, and handover events/opportunities. Handover events are counted from the declared prior-step incumbent using the engine's authoritative `beam_change`, `satellite_change`, and `cell_rekey` classifications. No demand cap is applied. Deadline numerator and denominator are both zero because the panel is not the online five-arm runner; consequently the scorer reports deadline-miss rate and per-arm timing/evaluation counts as unavailable instead of inventing them.
+
+The scorer's rigid v1 schema permits the reference object, information class, estimand, numerator, and energy boundary at panel identity/reference scope rather than alongside each scalar. The producer records them there, and the scorer copied them into every emitted result row. The exact numerator is:
+
+> sum of saturated full-buffer successfully decoded forward-downlink information bits; rate target is a power-control setpoint; no demand cap
+
+## Verified by running code
+
+### Scorer contract
+
+I read the complete validator in `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/scripts/score_stagec_checkpoints.py`, not only the cited lines. The producer follows its exact field inventories:
+
+- top level: `schema`, `panel_identity`, `reference_objects`, `coordinator_budget_s`, `runner_instrumentation`, `anchors`, `synthetic_smoke_not_evidence`, and `full_buffer_no_demand_cap`;
+- panel identity: `name`, `information_class`, `estimand`, `numerator`, `energy_boundary`, `anchors`, `worlds`, `dates`, `world_seeds`, `fixed_point_traversal_order`, and `provisioning_rule`;
+- the two reference objects and all anchor/profile/outcome inventories exactly as checked by the scorer;
+- coordinator budget exactly `10.0` seconds and a nonempty explicit fixed-point traversal order.
+
+The scorer file used for the dry run has SHA-256 `8a83bc9865fdbf665fe3815197059fc68c11efd73c319d96bcc412b5a8c5ed9d`. It was read and executed, not modified. `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/scripts/run_stagec_training.py` was not modified; its observed SHA-256 is `4885570b8552dc95a2143764cc10bd7b78f06504d63c4fa07866817bfc797d66`.
+
+### Exact anchor prefix
+
+The exact-source discovery authenticated both physics and view SHA-256 sidecars before accepting each anchor. Exactly the first 20 available entries in global generation order were used: global indices 000–019, comprising steps 0–5 for `nearest-eligible`, `stay-if-possible`, and `random-masked`, followed by step 6 for `nearest-eligible` and `stay-if-possible`. This is a prefix, not a selection. Their world is `V025_PROBE/world/1`, date is `2026-01-07`, and world seed is `5261619120743994529`.
+
+### Fixed point and 10-second incumbent
+
+The fixed-point traversal is deterministic cyclic first improvement:
+
+1. users in ascending user-ID order;
+2. each user's declared legal options in their declared order;
+3. candidates physically evaluated in ordered microbatches of 16;
+4. accept the first strict guarded-`F` improvement;
+5. terminate only after a complete final pass finds no strict improvement.
+
+PANELCEIL's completed authenticated receipt was available and was reused for global anchors 000–011. Its file SHA-256 is `52400cf180cd55f4b004be785ba4ff8021e09e38eba20cec7321fbad9999cf7d`, its internal receipt SHA-256 is `09e3e9c5e01f96bb879170ee1c31f752448f33fa6772284fabe8cbbea7fbceca`, and its path is `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ceiling30-ws/.scratch/panelceil/panelceil-receipt.json`. A post-build join verified that all 12 reused certified and 10-second endpoints match PANELCEIL exactly on bits, joules, served count, and rate-target-attained count.
+
+PANELCEIL covers only 12 anchors. For global anchors 012–019 the producer ran the same first-improvement implementation and required `termination_certificate.complete == true`; all eight passed. The 10-second reference is the last accepted fully evaluated iterate whose acceptance time is at most `10.0` seconds, not the base by definition and not the terminal certificate result by timing accident. The certified and 10-second profile identities differ on two of the 20 anchors.
+
+The construction receipt records 12 `PANELCEIL` reference sources, eight producer-computed sources, and complete fixed-point certificates for all 20.
+
+### Selector-latency reuse decision
+
+`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/receipts/selector-latency-full20.json` (SHA-256 `1f9ced246182820f0d8b8e54637a05333cc5a2bb3234f45b4de89b7a69cbabf9`) was inspected but not reused. It is a different panel: `V025_PROBE_R2/world/{1..4}`, five steps of `nearest-eligible`, whereas the requested exact-source prefix is `V025_PROBE/world/1` in three-carrier generation order. It also stores timing counts and selected commits, not the complete catalogue plus every profile's declared 48-boundary outcome. Reuse would therefore have changed both anchor identity and catalogue support.
+
+### Resource enforcement
+
+The producer used one Python process, `/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python`, niceness 15, and `OMP_NUM_THREADS`, `OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS`, `MKL_NUM_THREADS`, `NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS`, `VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS`, and `BLIS_NUM_THREADS` all equal to 1. It printed one `anchor k/N` progress line per anchor and peak-RSS lines. Producer peak RSS was `2,101,026,816` bytes, below 5 GB. The physical work recorded 960 feature-generation boundary evaluations and 949,248 full-outcome boundary evaluations. No more than one PANELBUILD Python process was run at once.
+
+### Real scorer dry run
+
+The final dry run used checkpoint:
+
+`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/.scratch/training-runner-checkpoint-kat-20260910-final/fixture-checkpoint/learner-6407676579069309528-epoch-000100.json`
